Skip a monitor with no mode when refreshing blur framebuffers

A blur refresh built the blur framebuffer of every monitor, including one
still connecting or left without a mode, whose transformed size is 0x0.
Allocating a 0x0 framebuffer trips the size assert in IFramebuffer::alloc
and aborts Hyprland. It happens when a monitor connects late at startup, and
when a monitor that dropped its link on wake reconnects and something, such
as a Lua config call, runs a refresh before the monitor has its mode.

Skip such a monitor. CMonitor::resources() rebuilds its resources once the
size changes, so it gets a blur framebuffer as soon as it has a mode.

Upstream: https://github.com/hyprwm/Hyprland/pull/16927 (1aa477bed3), merged
after 0.57.2. Drop it once the packaged release carries the fix.

--- a/src/config/supplementary/propRefresher/PropRefresher.cpp
+++ b/src/config/supplementary/propRefresher/PropRefresher.cpp
@@ -80,7 +80,7 @@ void CPropRefresher::refreshProp(const bool execdAsScheduled) {
         g_pHyprRenderer->refreshBlurProvider();
 
         for (auto const& m : State::monitorState()->monitors()) {
-            if (!m)
+            if (!m || m->m_transformedSize.x <= 0 || m->m_transformedSize.y <= 0)
                 continue;
 
             m->resources()->refreshBlurFB();
